    <string name="battery_ok_sub">The progress notification can start with the app closed.</string>
    <string name="battery_restricted">Battery optimisation limits PrintCtrl</string>
    <string name="battery_restricted_sub">Tap to allow it. Without this, the progress notification only starts while the app is open.</string>
    <string name="battery_coloros">ColorOS: allow auto launch and background activity</string>
    <string name="battery_coloros_sub">On OPPO and OnePlus phones, open Battery in the app\'s settings and choose \"Allow background activity\", and turn on auto launch, or ColorOS stops the checks.</string>
    <string name="battery_footer">PrintCtrl doesn\'t use Google\'s push service, so Android has to let it run now and then to check your printers.</string>

